---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../content/site.json';

const askEnabled = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ASK_ENABLED === 'true';
---

<Base
  paper
  title={`Privacy | ${site.name}`}
  description={`How ${site.name}'s portfolio handles the information you share.`}
>
  <article class="doc container">
    <a class="link doc__back" href="/">
      <svg class="i" aria-hidden="true">
        <use href="#i-arrow"></use>
      </svg>{' '}
      Back to the dimension
    </a>
    <header class="doc__head">
      <h1 class="doc__title">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="doc__intro">Short version: no cookies, no tracking, and your messages are only used to reply to you.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Contact form</h2>
      <p>
        The form asks for your name, email, project type, an optional budget and your message. It's used only to reply
        to your enquiry. Depending on how the site is configured, sending either opens your own email app with the
        message pre-filled, or delivers it to {site.name}'s inbox through a form-delivery service (Web3Forms or
        Formspree) that processes the message on {site.name}'s behalf.
      </p>
      <h2>Email and WhatsApp</h2>
      <p>Links to email and WhatsApp open those services directly; their own privacy policies apply.</p>
      {askEnabled && (
        <>
          <h2>AI assistant</h2>
          <p>
            Questions you type into the assistant are sent to Anthropic's Claude API to generate an answer from this
            site's published information. Message text isn't stored by this site. Please don't share personal or
            sensitive information there.
          </p>
        </>
      )}
      <h2>Settings stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        If you change the motion or 3D settings, that preference is saved in your browser's local storage so it's
        remembered next time. Nothing is sent anywhere.
      </p>
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
